{"schemaVersion":{"minor":3,"major":0,"patch":0},"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Send each batch of records to an HTTP endpoint, and send it again until it arrives."}],"sections":[],"kind":"symbol","topicSections":[{"identifiers":["doc:\/\/HTTPDestinations\/documentation\/HTTPDestinations\/HTTPDestination","doc:\/\/HTTPDestinations\/documentation\/HTTPDestinations\/HTTPDropReport"],"title":"Sending batches","anchor":"Sending-batches"},{"identifiers":["doc:\/\/HTTPDestinations\/documentation\/HTTPDestinations\/BatchEncoder","doc:\/\/HTTPDestinations\/documentation\/HTTPDestinations\/EncodedBatch"],"title":"Encoding a batch","anchor":"Encoding-a-batch"},{"identifiers":["doc:\/\/HTTPDestinations\/documentation\/HTTPDestinations\/ResponseOutcome","doc:\/\/HTTPDestinations\/documentation\/HTTPDestinations\/HTTPTransportResponse"],"title":"Reading a 2xx answer","anchor":"Reading-a-2xx-answer"},{"identifiers":["doc:\/\/HTTPDestinations\/documentation\/HTTPDestinations\/BatchRequests","doc:\/\/HTTPDestinations\/documentation\/HTTPDestinations\/EncodedRequest","doc:\/\/HTTPDestinations\/documentation\/HTTPDestinations\/SkippedRecord"],"title":"Splitting a batch into requests","anchor":"Splitting-a-batch-into-requests"},{"identifiers":["doc:\/\/HTTPDestinations\/documentation\/HTTPDestinations\/TransientStatus","doc:\/\/HTTPDestinations\/documentation\/HTTPDestinations\/InvalidTransientStatus"],"title":"Retrying a vendor’s own statuses","anchor":"Retrying-a-vendors-own-statuses"},{"identifiers":["doc:\/\/HTTPDestinations\/documentation\/HTTPDestinations\/ExponentialBackoff","doc:\/\/HTTPDestinations\/documentation\/HTTPDestinations\/InvalidBackoff","doc:\/\/HTTPDestinations\/documentation\/HTTPDestinations\/NonPositiveRetry"],"title":"Waiting between attempts","anchor":"Waiting-between-attempts"},{"identifiers":["doc:\/\/HTTPDestinations\/documentation\/HTTPDestinations\/HTTPTransport","doc:\/\/HTTPDestinations\/documentation\/HTTPDestinations\/URLSessionTransport","doc:\/\/HTTPDestinations\/documentation\/HTTPDestinations\/HTTPTransportError"],"title":"Sending requests","anchor":"Sending-requests"}],"identifier":{"url":"doc:\/\/HTTPDestinations\/documentation\/HTTPDestinations","interfaceLanguage":"swift"},"hierarchy":{"paths":[[]]},"metadata":{"title":"HTTPDestinations","symbolKind":"module","modules":[{"name":"HTTPDestinations"}],"roleHeading":"Framework","role":"collection","externalID":"HTTPDestinations"},"variants":[{"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}],"paths":["\/documentation\/httpdestinations"]}],"primaryContentSections":[{"content":[{"anchor":"Overview","level":2,"type":"heading","text":"Overview"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/HTTPDestinations\/documentation\/HTTPDestinations\/HTTPDestination","type":"reference"},{"text":" is a destination that posts each batch it receives as the requests its","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/HTTPDestinations\/documentation\/HTTPDestinations\/BatchEncoder","type":"reference"},{"text":" splits it into: one request for an endpoint without limits. Each body is whatever","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"the encoder writes for its records, so events need no ","type":"text"},{"code":"Codable","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" conformance and the wire format is","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"yours. It sends with ","type":"text"},{"code":"URLSession","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" through","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/HTTPDestinations\/documentation\/HTTPDestinations\/URLSessionTransport","type":"reference"},{"text":" by default, or through any ","type":"text"},{"isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/HTTPDestinations\/documentation\/HTTPDestinations\/HTTPTransport","type":"reference"},{"text":" you pass.","type":"text"}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"A send that gets no response, or a 5xx, 408 or 429 status, is sent again after the next wait of its"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"reference","isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/HTTPDestinations\/documentation\/HTTPDestinations\/ExponentialBackoff"},{"type":"text","text":": nominally 1 second, doubling up to 60 seconds, unless you pass another. So"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"is one answered with a status the encoder lists in "},{"type":"reference","isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/HTTPDestinations\/documentation\/HTTPDestinations\/BatchEncoder\/transientStatuses"},{"type":"text","text":", which every"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"encoder declares: empty for most servers, or each other failure its vendor answers to a request"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"worth sending again, such as Aptabase’s 418 for a slow upload."}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"A 2xx counts as delivered unless the encoder’s "},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/HTTPDestinations\/documentation\/HTTPDestinations\/BatchEncoder\/outcome(of:for:)","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"type":"text","text":" reads its body and"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"says otherwise. Some vendors answer 200 to a request they didn’t store, and say so only in the"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"body: Mixpanel’s "},{"code":"{\"status\": 0}","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":", or Aptabase’s "},{"code":"{\"error\": ...}","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" for an unknown key. A 2xx the"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"encoder reads as "},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/HTTPDestinations\/documentation\/HTTPDestinations\/ResponseOutcome\/rejected(reason:)","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"type":"text","text":" is dropped and reported as"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/HTTPDestinations\/documentation\/HTTPDestinations\/HTTPDropReport\/rejectedInBody(status:reason:recordIDs:)","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"type":"text","text":". One it reads as"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/HTTPDestinations\/documentation\/HTTPDestinations\/ResponseOutcome\/transient(reason:)","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"type":"text","text":" is sent again under the same backoff and deadline as a 5xx."},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"An encoder should count an empty body, or one it can’t read, as delivered, so an answer it"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"doesn’t recognize never sends a request again and again; the DestinationTesting conformance kit"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"checks that it does. A transient answer is retried until the request’s deadline, so an encoder"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"whose requests have none should return rejected instead."}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"Each wait has full jitter by default: a random wait shorter than the nominal one, so apps refused","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"at the same moment retry at different moments. Pass ","type":"text"},{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/HTTPDestinations\/documentation\/HTTPDestinations\/ExponentialBackoff\/Jitter-swift.enum\/none","isActive":true},{"text":" for the","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"nominal waits. In tests, pass a seeded generator as ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"randomNumberGenerator:"},{"text":" for jittered waits","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"that repeat from one run to the next, as long as one request retries at a time: copies of a","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"destination retrying at once share the generator’s draws in the order they ask for them. Never","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"seed it in production, where every device would then wait the same, which defeats the jitter. The","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"destination takes the next batch only once this one is delivered or dropped, so a tracker’s store","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"keeps the batch’s records until then. A batch the endpoint answers with any other status, whose","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"request can never be sent, or that the encoder can’t encode is dropped, logged and reported on","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/HTTPDestinations\/documentation\/HTTPDestinations\/HTTPDestination\/dropReports","isActive":true},{"text":" as an ","type":"text"},{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/HTTPDestinations\/documentation\/HTTPDestinations\/HTTPDropReport","isActive":true},{"text":", as is each record the encoder leaves out","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"of its requests. So is a request still undelivered at its ","type":"text"},{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/HTTPDestinations\/documentation\/HTTPDestinations\/EncodedRequest\/deadline","isActive":true},{"text":", which an","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"encoder sets for a vendor that misdates or ignores old events: the destination checks it on its","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"now:"},{"text":" clock before every attempt and sends nothing more once it has passed.","type":"text"}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The tracing instrument injects the trace context of each request’s first record into its header"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"fields, and "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Content-Type"},{"type":"text","text":" is always the encoder’s."}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"Reach for this module to send to a server whose format you write yourself. For TraffluentCollector’s","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"format, give the destination a ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"CollectorBatchEncoder"},{"text":" (module ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"CollectorEncoding"},{"text":"); for PostHog,","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"make it with ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"HTTPDestination.postHog(projectToken:host:plan:)"},{"text":" (module ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"PostHogEncoding"},{"text":"); for","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"Amplitude, with ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"HTTPDestination.amplitude(apiKey:region:plan:)"},{"text":" (module ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"AmplitudeEncoding"},{"text":"); for","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"Mixpanel, with ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"HTTPDestination.mixpanel(projectToken:region:plan:)"},{"text":" (module ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"MixpanelEncoding"},{"text":");","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"for Segment, RudderStack or Customer.io Data Pipelines, with","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"HTTPDestination.segment(writeKey:region:plan:)"},{"text":", ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"rudderStack(writeKey:dataPlane:plan:)"},{"text":" or","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"customerIO(apiKey:region:plan:)"},{"text":" (module ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"SegmentSpecEncoding"},{"text":"); for Google Analytics 4, from a","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"server, with ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"HTTPDestination.googleAnalytics(measurementID:apiSecret:region:plan:)"},{"text":" (module","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"GoogleAnalyticsEncoding"},{"text":"); for Snowplow, with","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"HTTPDestination.snowplow(collector:vendor:appID:plan:)"},{"text":" (module ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"SnowplowEncoding"},{"text":"); for","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"TelemetryDeck, with ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"HTTPDestination.telemetryDeck(appID:namespace:testMode:plan:)"},{"text":" (module","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"TelemetryDeckEncoding"},{"text":"); for Matomo, with","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"HTTPDestination.matomo(url:siteID:dimensions:category:plan:)"},{"text":" (module ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"MatomoEncoding"},{"text":"); for","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"Heap, with ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"HTTPDestination.heap(appID:region:plan:)"},{"text":" (module ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"HeapEncoding"},{"text":"); for Aptabase, with","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"HTTPDestination.aptabase(appKey:host:isDebug:plan:)"},{"text":" (module ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"AptabaseEncoding"},{"text":"). To read events","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"inside the app or in a test, use","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"InMemoryDestination"},{"text":" (module ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Destinations"},{"text":") instead.","type":"text"}]},{"code":["import HTTPDestinations","","struct PlansEncoder: BatchEncoder {","    static let transientStatuses: Set<TransientStatus> = []","","    static func outcome(of response: HTTPTransportResponse, for request: EncodedRequest) -> ResponseOutcome {","        .delivered","    }","","    func requests(for batch: [EventRecord]) -> BatchRequests<Never> {","        let plans = batch.compactMap { ($0.event as? SignedUp)?.plan }","        let body = EncodedBatch(body: Data(plans.joined(separator: \"\\n\").utf8), contentType: \"text\/plain\")","        return BatchRequests(requests: [EncodedRequest(body: body, recordIDs: batch.map(\\.id))], skippedRecords: [])","    }","}","","let server = HTTPDestination(","    endpoint: endpointURL,","    headerFields: [.authorization: \"Bearer \\(token)\"],","    encoder: PlansEncoder(),","    backoff: try ExponentialBackoff(initialDelay: .seconds(2), maximumDelay: .seconds(120)))","let drops = server.dropReports","let watching = Task {","    for await drop in drops {","        print(\"Dropped a batch: \\(drop)\")","    }","}","let delivery = tracker.records.batch().deliver(to: server)"],"syntax":"swift","type":"codeListing"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"The guide ","type":"text"},{"isActive":true,"identifier":"https:\/\/tyler-keith-thompson.github.io\/Traffluent\/documentation\/traffluent\/choosingdestinations","type":"reference"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"covers this destination beside the others, and what a delivery does while a batch is retried.","type":"text"}]}],"kind":"content"}],"references":{"doc://HTTPDestinations/documentation/HTTPDestinations/ExponentialBackoff/delay(beforeRetry:)":{"fragments":[{"text":"func","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"delay","kind":"identifier"},{"text":"(","kind":"text"},{"text":"beforeRetry","kind":"externalParam"},{"text":": ","kind":"text"},{"preciseIdentifier":"s:Si","text":"Int","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":") ","kind":"text"},{"text":"throws","kind":"keyword"},{"text":"(","kind":"text"},{"preciseIdentifier":"s:16HTTPDestinations16NonPositiveRetryV","text":"NonPositiveRetry","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":") -> ","kind":"text"},{"preciseIdentifier":"s:s8DurationV","text":"Duration","kind":"typeIdentifier"}],"type":"topic","abstract":[{"text":"The nominal wait before retry number ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"retry"},{"text":": ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"initialDelay"},{"text":" doubled ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"retry - 1"},{"text":" times, or","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"maximumDelay"},{"text":" if that is less.","type":"text"}],"identifier":"doc:\/\/HTTPDestinations\/documentation\/HTTPDestinations\/ExponentialBackoff\/delay(beforeRetry:)","kind":"symbol","url":"\/documentation\/httpdestinations\/exponentialbackoff\/delay(beforeretry:)","title":"delay(beforeRetry:)","role":"symbol"},"doc://HTTPDestinations/documentation/HTTPDestinations/URLSessionTransport":{"fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"struct"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"URLSessionTransport"}],"url":"\/documentation\/httpdestinations\/urlsessiontransport","title":"URLSessionTransport","navigatorTitle":[{"kind":"identifier","text":"URLSessionTransport"}],"type":"topic","identifier":"doc:\/\/HTTPDestinations\/documentation\/HTTPDestinations\/URLSessionTransport","kind":"symbol","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"An "},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/HTTPDestinations\/documentation\/HTTPDestinations\/HTTPTransport","type":"reference","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":" that sends each request with a "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"URLSession"},{"type":"text","text":"."}],"role":"symbol"},"doc://HTTPDestinations/documentation/HTTPDestinations/ExponentialBackoff/Jitter-swift.enum/none":{"url":"\/documentation\/httpdestinations\/exponentialbackoff\/jitter-swift.enum\/none","identifier":"doc:\/\/HTTPDestinations\/documentation\/HTTPDestinations\/ExponentialBackoff\/Jitter-swift.enum\/none","type":"topic","kind":"symbol","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"The nominal wait, exactly."}],"fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"case"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"none"}],"role":"symbol","title":"ExponentialBackoff.Jitter.none"},"doc://HTTPDestinations/documentation/HTTPDestinations/BatchEncoder":{"navigatorTitle":[{"kind":"identifier","text":"BatchEncoder"}],"fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"protocol"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"BatchEncoder"}],"identifier":"doc:\/\/HTTPDestinations\/documentation\/HTTPDestinations\/BatchEncoder","role":"symbol","type":"topic","abstract":[{"text":"What turns a batch of records into the requests ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/HTTPDestinations\/documentation\/HTTPDestinations\/HTTPDestination","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"text":" sends.","type":"text"}],"url":"\/documentation\/httpdestinations\/batchencoder","kind":"symbol","title":"BatchEncoder"},"https://tyler-keith-thompson.github.io/Traffluent/documentation/traffluent/choosingdestinations":{"titleInlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Choosing Destinations"}],"identifier":"https:\/\/tyler-keith-thompson.github.io\/Traffluent\/documentation\/traffluent\/choosingdestinations","title":"Choosing Destinations","type":"link","url":"https:\/\/tyler-keith-thompson.github.io\/Traffluent\/documentation\/traffluent\/choosingdestinations"},"doc://HTTPDestinations/documentation/HTTPDestinations/TransientStatus":{"fragments":[{"text":"struct","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"TransientStatus","kind":"identifier"}],"url":"\/documentation\/httpdestinations\/transientstatus","title":"TransientStatus","navigatorTitle":[{"text":"TransientStatus","kind":"identifier"}],"type":"topic","identifier":"doc:\/\/HTTPDestinations\/documentation\/HTTPDestinations\/TransientStatus","kind":"symbol","abstract":[{"text":"A failure status that ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/HTTPDestinations\/documentation\/HTTPDestinations\/HTTPDestination","type":"reference","isActive":true},{"text":" retries, beside 408 Request Timeout, 429 Too Many","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"Requests and every 5xx, for an encoder that lists it in ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/HTTPDestinations\/documentation\/HTTPDestinations\/BatchEncoder\/transientStatuses","type":"reference","isActive":true},{"text":".","type":"text"}],"role":"symbol"},"doc://HTTPDestinations/documentation/HTTPDestinations/HTTPTransportResponse":{"kind":"symbol","role":"symbol","identifier":"doc:\/\/HTTPDestinations\/documentation\/HTTPDestinations\/HTTPTransportResponse","type":"topic","navigatorTitle":[{"text":"HTTPTransportResponse","kind":"identifier"}],"abstract":[{"text":"What an ","type":"text"},{"isActive":true,"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/HTTPDestinations\/documentation\/HTTPDestinations\/HTTPTransport"},{"text":" received for a request: the response’s status and header fields, and","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"its body.","type":"text"}],"url":"\/documentation\/httpdestinations\/httptransportresponse","title":"HTTPTransportResponse","fragments":[{"text":"struct","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"HTTPTransportResponse","kind":"identifier"}]},"doc://HTTPDestinations/documentation/HTTPDestinations/ExponentialBackoff":{"navigatorTitle":[{"text":"ExponentialBackoff","kind":"identifier"}],"url":"\/documentation\/httpdestinations\/exponentialbackoff","identifier":"doc:\/\/HTTPDestinations\/documentation\/HTTPDestinations\/ExponentialBackoff","type":"topic","abstract":[{"text":"How long ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/HTTPDestinations\/documentation\/HTTPDestinations\/HTTPDestination","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"text":" waits before each new attempt at a batch that wasn’t delivered:","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"binary exponential backoff, each nominal wait twice the one before, up to a maximum, with","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"jitter.","type":"text"}],"kind":"symbol","fragments":[{"text":"struct","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"ExponentialBackoff","kind":"identifier"}],"role":"symbol","title":"ExponentialBackoff"},"doc://HTTPDestinations/documentation/HTTPDestinations/EncodedRequest/deadline":{"url":"\/documentation\/httpdestinations\/encodedrequest\/deadline","kind":"symbol","fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"var"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"deadline"},{"kind":"text","text":": "},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:20FoundationEssentials4DateV","text":"Date"},{"kind":"text","text":"?"}],"role":"symbol","type":"topic","identifier":"doc:\/\/HTTPDestinations\/documentation\/HTTPDestinations\/EncodedRequest\/deadline","title":"deadline","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"The latest wall-clock time at which the request may be sent, or "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"nil"},{"type":"text","text":" when it may be sent"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"at any time."}]},"doc://HTTPDestinations/documentation/HTTPDestinations/HTTPDropReport":{"title":"HTTPDropReport","url":"\/documentation\/httpdestinations\/httpdropreport","navigatorTitle":[{"text":"HTTPDropReport","kind":"identifier"}],"fragments":[{"text":"enum","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"HTTPDropReport","kind":"identifier"}],"role":"symbol","type":"topic","identifier":"doc:\/\/HTTPDestinations\/documentation\/HTTPDestinations\/HTTPDropReport","kind":"symbol","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"A batch "},{"type":"reference","isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/HTTPDestinations\/documentation\/HTTPDestinations\/HTTPDestination"},{"type":"text","text":" dropped without delivering it, and why."}]},"doc://HTTPDestinations/documentation/HTTPDestinations/ResponseOutcome":{"type":"topic","role":"symbol","fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"enum"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"ResponseOutcome"}],"identifier":"doc:\/\/HTTPDestinations\/documentation\/HTTPDestinations\/ResponseOutcome","navigatorTitle":[{"kind":"identifier","text":"ResponseOutcome"}],"title":"ResponseOutcome","url":"\/documentation\/httpdestinations\/responseoutcome","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"What a successful (2xx) answer to a request means, as its "},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/HTTPDestinations\/documentation\/HTTPDestinations\/BatchEncoder","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"type":"text","text":" reads the answer